From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: per-plane IGC and 3D LUT color pipelines

The VIG pipes of SM8550, SM8650 and SM8750 carry an inverse gamma LUT
(IGC v6, 257 samples) and a 17^3 3D LUT (gamut v6.1) ahead of blending.
Expose them as a DRM plane color pipeline, 1D LUT -> 3D LUT, so a
compositor can give each plane its own transform: an HDR10 layer and an
SDR overlay on the same frame no longer need a GPU composition pass to
reach one output encoding.

Both blocks load only through LUTDMA, from its double-buffered queue:
the per-CTL queue 0, started by a software trigger in the CTL rather than
by a flush, so the commit runs it from atomic_flush and waits for it
before the CTL flush latches the pipe. The engine gains that queue for
both of its layouts (v2 on SM8550, v3 on SM8650 and SM8750). The gamut
table streams over the LUT bus in the same node and component order as
the DSPP gamut, 10 bits MSB aligned; the IGC goes through its index and
data ports with c0, c1, c2 carrying green, blue, red, as the DSPP IGC
does. Addresses in the queue are relative to the pipe's LUTDMA window,
which starts 0xa00 (SM8550) or 0x700 (SM8650, SM8750) into the pipe. Each
block has two banks; the idle one is written and the opmode, shared by
both blocks, switches to it, so a load never tears. A transfer that times
out stops further loads until the power domain resets the engine.

A plane with an active pipeline needs a VIG with the blocks and cannot
share a pipe through multirect (the second rect has no LUT blocks). Each
pipe remembers the blobs it holds so an unchanged plane is not reloaded;
the memory is dropped on runtime resume, when the power domain has lost
the LUT RAM.

---
diff -ruN a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -1070,9 +1070,27 @@
 		dpu_plane_flush(plane);
 	}
 
+	if (dpu_crtc->luts_queued) {
+		struct dpu_hw_ctl *ctl = cstate->mixers[0].lm_ctl;
+
+		dpu_crtc->luts_queued = false;
+		if (dpu_reg_dma_flush_db(_dpu_crtc_get_kms(crtc)->reg_dma, ctl->idx, &ctl->hw))
+			DRM_ERROR_RATELIMITED("crtc%d pipe LUT load timed out\n", crtc->base.id);
+	}
+
 	/* Kickoff will be scheduled by outer layer */
 }
 
+int dpu_crtc_lut_ctl_idx(struct drm_crtc *crtc)
+{
+	struct dpu_crtc_state *cstate = to_dpu_crtc_state(crtc->state);
+
+	if (!cstate->num_mixers)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	to_dpu_crtc(crtc)->luts_queued = true;
+	return cstate->mixers[0].lm_ctl->idx;
+}
+
 /**
  * dpu_crtc_destroy_state - state destroy hook
  * @crtc: drm CRTC
